From aa4df0e78a0ddf0271de46ea915b54700f145e21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:51:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vc4: Use the HVS field bit for interlaced scanout
 position

vc4_crtc_get_scanout_position() adds half a line to hpos on one of the
two fields of an interlaced mode, and picks that field from the parity
of the HVS frame counter. The frame counter is free running and is not
cleared when the channel is reset, so its parity has no fixed relation
to the field being output. Depending on the history of the channel the
correction lands on the wrong field, and the vblank timestamps then
alternate by two lines.

The HVS status register already read in this function reports the
active field: SCALER6_DISPX_STATUS_OFIELD on BCM2712, and bit 27 of
SCALER_DISPSTATX on earlier generations. Use it instead. The correction
applies when the bit is clear.

Measured as the median change between consecutive vblank timestamp
intervals over 200 fields, with 1080i60, 1080i50, 480i and 576i on
HDMI, and NTSC and PAL on Pi 4 composite:

  - frame counter parity: 0 or 2 lines, depending on the modeset
    (Pi 5 and Pi 4; Pi 3 happened to be right in every run)
  - field bit, set: 2 lines on Pi 3, Pi 4 and Pi 5
  - field bit, clear: 0-2 us on Pi 3, Pi 4 and Pi 5 in every run

Fixes: e538092cb15c ("drm/vc4: Enable precise vblank timestamping for interlaced modes.")
Fixes: 7687a12153d3 ("drm/vc4: hvs: Add support for BCM2712 HVS")
Link: https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/issues/7757
Signed-off-by: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_crtc.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_regs.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_crtc.c
@@ -153,10 +153,20 @@ static bool vc4_crtc_get_scanout_positio
 	*hpos = 0;
 
 	if (mode->flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_INTERLACE) {
+		bool field;
+
 		*vpos /= 2;
 
-		/* Use hpos to correct for field offset in interlaced mode. */
-		if (vc4_hvs_get_fifo_frame_count(hvs, channel) % 2)
+		if (vc4->gen >= VC4_GEN_6_C)
+			field = val & SCALER6_DISPX_STATUS_OFIELD;
+		else
+			field = val & SCALER_DISPSTATX_FIELD;
+
+		/*
+		 * Use hpos to correct for field offset in interlaced mode.
+		 * The offset applies when the field bit is clear.
+		 */
+		if (!field)
 			*hpos += mode->crtc_htotal / 2;
 	}
 
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_regs.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_regs.h
@@ -421,6 +421,7 @@
 # define SCALER_DISPSTATX_MODE_EOF		3
 # define SCALER_DISPSTATX_FULL			BIT(29)
 # define SCALER_DISPSTATX_EMPTY			BIT(28)
+# define SCALER_DISPSTATX_FIELD			BIT(27)
 # define SCALER_DISPSTATX_LINE_MASK		VC4_MASK(11, 0)
 # define SCALER_DISPSTATX_LINE_SHIFT		0
 
